1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Display
X-ray, wire, hide and show, isolate, border edges, color

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.883
The Display section holds what Maya keeps in the Display menu and in the shelf.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:14.317
X-ray makes only the selected objects see-through; the slider next to it sets the opacity.

4
00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:19.750
Wire on shaded: the wireframe over the solid shading, like Maya's Wireframe on Shaded.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.183
Hide hides the selection. Show sel shows the hidden objects selected in the Outliner, Show last the last hidden group, Show all everything.

6
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.617
In Edit Mode the same buttons work on components: they hide and show faces.

7
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:36.050
Isolate is Blender's Local View: only the selection. Again to return. In Edit Mode it hides the rest of the mesh.

8
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.483
Border edges draws the open edges in orange: the mesh's borders and holes. Underneath, width and color; Select border edges selects them in Edit Mode.

9
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:46.917
Object color: eight colors and a free one for the selected objects, X goes back to white. It switches the viewport shading to Object.

10
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:49.850
Display

